                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237794302",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198098404029",
                            "num_reviews": 21,
                            "playtime_forever": 184,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 184,
                            "last_played": 1792091419
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game has its charms, but there's a few problems that prevent me from recommending it:\n*The flight and gliding controls feel wonky and take some time to get used to.\n*The game's too hard for its own good, later you'll deal with enemies that deal almost unavoidable damage and trap you in unwinnable death loops.\n*Later on in the game, you simply don't get enough health pickups, leading to said unwinnable death loops.\n*I didn't get to him, but I hear final boss is quite the difficulty spike.\n\nI had to quit my run through since I got in an unwinnable death loop and tried to get the good ending, which requires giving up your fire breath. Problem is, there's no way I was getting past where I was at without said fire breath. I'd have to start a new game due to the game's save system. It's a short game, but it's just *maddening*.\n\nEdit: Finally beat the final boss: he sucked as much as I expected. This game would be more charming if the difficulty wasn't so high, I think. It's a shame. :(",
